WEBVTT

0
00:00:00.009 --> 00:00:01.000
Exercise 2,

1
00:00:01.370 --> 00:00:05.289
create a timer using set interval and clear it when the component unmounts.

2
00:00:06.079 --> 00:00:06.300
OK,

3
00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:06.980
let's do it.

4
00:00:07.239 --> 00:00:09.279
We have a component called XC2.

5
00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:10.960
Inside the component,

6
00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:13.229
we have a counter with count set to 0

7
00:00:13.430 --> 00:00:15.170
and a function set count to update it.

8
00:00:15.939 --> 00:00:16.350
Next,

9
00:00:16.459 --> 00:00:17.979
we return the timer value,

10
00:00:18.110 --> 00:00:18.989
which is the count.

11
00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:20.020
Now,

12
00:00:20.319 --> 00:00:21.479
let's add the use effect.

13
00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:23.579
Inside the use effect,

14
00:00:23.860 --> 00:00:25.739
declare a timer using set interval.

15
00:00:26.430 --> 00:00:29.870
The set interval function increments the counter by 1 every second.

16
00:00:30.629 --> 00:00:31.940
To prevent memory leaks,

17
00:00:32.189 --> 00:00:34.069
don't forget to return a cleanup function.

18
00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:36.259
The cleanup function uses

19
00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:38.419
clear interval to stop the timer

20
00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:40.159
when the component unmounts.

21
00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:41.880
Let's see it in action.

22
00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:43.830
We'll open the terminal,

23
00:00:44.119 --> 00:00:46.840
run the project again using NPM RundDev,

24
00:00:47.319 --> 00:00:50.000
and take the URL to open it in the browser.

25
00:00:59.650 --> 00:01:00.349
And now

26
00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:02.110
you can see the timer working,

27
00:01:02.279 --> 00:01:04.129
incrementing every second.

28
00:01:04.888 --> 00:01:05.589
Have a good day

29
00:01:06.050 --> 00:01:07.650
and see you in the next lesson.